;; RETIRED in 0.4.52 (owner: Simon's crypt has a new way in, from 5-1): no level leads here any
;; more (5-4's lift is a plain lift again in the campaign too), so it is reached only from the
;; developer level select. Kept, with its id, for the cracked wall, the Koopa that comes back and
;; their tests (tests/sim/simon-crypt.test.ts); an area of 5-1 since then, as the crypt below it.
;; It was Simon's dungeon under the 5-4 lift shaft (riding 5-4's down lift on past the screen
;; bottom carried the player down here, the shaft's `descent` zone; level/campaign.ts).
;; One screen: the player drops in at the right; a single hard block (11,10) stands between the
;; landing and a Koopa pacing up to the CRACKED WALL (column 5, rows 8-10, `&`). Any hero attack
;; breaks the wall; a hero with no attack stomps the Koopa and kicks its shell into it (kicked the
;; wrong way, the shell bounces off the block and comes back to the wall). The Koopa comes back
;; if lost while the wall stands (`respawn`). Behind the wall, steps lead down to a hole: the
;; drop into Simon's crypt. The clock runs on (time: inherit).

[tiles]
